examples.solution_text:
(a)
$\begin{align*}3x+2&\le11\\3x&\le9\\x&\le3\end{align*}$
The closed circle includes $3$; the arrow points left towards smaller values.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"inequality-closed-left-straight-ray"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-6,-7) rectangle (86,10.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,<->] (-4,0)--(84,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ({8*(\v+5)},-1.3)--({8*(\v+5)},1.3);
\node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at ({8*(\v+5)},-1.3) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\v$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};
}
\draw[black,line width=1.2pt,->] (64,0)--(-4,0);
\fill[black] (64,0) circle[radius=1];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) Divide by $-2$ and reverse the symbol.
$\begin{align*}5-2x&<9\\-2x&<4\\x&>-2\end{align*}$
The open circle excludes $-2$; the arrow points right towards larger values.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"inequality-open-right-straight-ray"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-6,-7) rectangle (86,10.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,<->] (-4,0)--(84,0);
\foreach \v in {-5,...,5} {
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ({8*(\v+5)},-1.3)--({8*(\v+5)},1.3);
\node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at ({8*(\v+5)},-1.3) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\v$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};
}
\draw[black,line width=1.2pt,->] (24,0)--(84,0);
\draw[black,fill=white,line width=0.8pt] (24,0) circle[radius=1];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The outward arrowheads indicate that each solution set continues indefinitely.

Dividing by a negative number reverses the inequality symbol.
$\begin{align*}-2x&\ge8\\x&\le-4\end{align*}$
Correct solution: a closed circle at $-4$ with an arrow pointing left.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"diagnosis-correct-left-straight-ray"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-6,-7) rectangle (86,10.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,<->] (-4,0)--(84,0);
\foreach \v in {-8,...,2} {
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ({8*(\v+8)},-1.3)--({8*(\v+8)},1.3);
\node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at ({8*(\v+8)},-1.3) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\v$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};
}
\draw[black,line width=1.2pt,->] (32,0)--(-4,0);
\fill[black] (32,0) circle[radius=1];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Student's answer, $x\ge-4$: a closed circle at $-4$ with an arrow pointing right.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[],"reference":"diagnosis-incorrect-right-straight-ray"}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1mm,y=1mm]
\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes="1"/>}
\path[use as bounding box] (-6,-7) rectangle (86,10.3);
\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,<->] (-4,0)--(84,0);
\foreach \v in {-8,...,2} {
\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] ({8*(\v+8)},-1.3)--({8*(\v+8)},1.3);
\node[below,text=black,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at ({8*(\v+8)},-1.3) {\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text="tick">}$\v$\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};
}
\draw[black,line width=1.2pt,->] (32,0)--(84,0);
\fill[black] (32,0) circle[radius=1];
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The outward arrowheads indicate indefinite continuation. The two sets extend in opposite directions and share only $x=-4$.
